      {
        "type": "block",
        "id": "t70",
        "label": "The condition shown is caused by a single gene. II-4 married into the family; in the wider population 1 person in 25 is a carrier.\n(a)  Is the condition dominant or recessive, autosomal or sex-linked? Give the evidence from the pedigree, not from the shading.\n(b)  Why must I-1 and I-2 both be carriers, while II-1 and II-3 only might be?      (c)  What is P(II-3 is a carrier)?\n(d)  Find the probability that III-1 is a carrier.      (e)  What is the chance that III-1 and III-2 are both carriers?",
        "x": 46,
        "y": 721.4,
        "width": 1040,
        "height": 85,
